    body: [
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "Hello, Anik! You are always busy with your mobile phone. What are you doing?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "Hello, Tamim. I am just chatting with some friends on Messenger." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "At eleven in the morning, with the test examination only a month away?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "Why not? A mobile phone is a wonderful thing. We cannot do without it today." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "I agree that it is a wonderful invention, but it has both uses and abuses." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "Tell me about its uses first." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "It has made communication very easy and cheap. We can talk to anyone at any time, in any part of the world. In an emergency we can call a doctor, the police or the fire service at once." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "And it is not only a telephone now. It has a camera, a calculator, a clock and a radio in it." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "Right. A smartphone is almost a small computer. We can browse the internet, read books, attend online classes and see our results on it." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "My father sends money to my brother in Dhaka through bKash in a minute." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "Yes, mobile banking has made money transactions quick and safe. Farmers learn the market price of their crops, and businessmen run their business with its help. It has truly made the world a global village." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "Then where is the abuse?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "The abuse lies in how we use it. Many students, like you, waste hours on chatting, games and videos. They become addicted and neglect their studies." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "I must confess that I sometimes use it till two o'clock at night." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "That is harmful to your health. Using it for a long time causes headache, weak eyesight and insomnia. Some doctors believe that its radiation may also harm the brain." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "That is alarming. Are there any other abuses?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "Many. Criminals use it for kidnapping, blackmailing and cheating people. Some people harass girls with indecent calls and messages, and rumours spread through it very fast." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "I have also seen people talking on the phone while driving or crossing the road." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "That causes many accidents. Some students even use it to cheat in the examination hall." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "So it can be a blessing or a curse, depending on the user." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "Exactly. We should use it with moderation and only when it is necessary. Students should keep it away while studying and at bedtime." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "You are right. From today I shall use my phone only for an hour in the evening." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Tamim", text: "That is a wise decision. I wish you success." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Anik", text: "Thank you, Tamim. Goodbye." },
    ],
