    body: [
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Hello, Rafi! Have you read today's newspaper?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Not yet. Is there any important news?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "A bus fell into a roadside ditch on the Dhaka-Aricha highway yesterday. Twelve people were killed and more than thirty injured." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "How sad! Road accidents have become a daily affair in our country." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Yes. Thousands of people die on our roads every year, and many more are crippled for life. Why do so many accidents happen?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "There are many causes. The first is reckless driving. Drivers drive at high speed and try to overtake one another dangerously." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Many of them have no proper training either." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Right. A large number of drivers are untrained, and some of them have no valid licence. Some drive for long hours without rest, and some even drive under the influence of drugs." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "What about the vehicles?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Many buses and trucks are old and unfit for the road. Their brakes and lights do not work properly. Besides, they are often overloaded with passengers and goods." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Our roads are also narrow and full of holes." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "That is another cause. Many roads have dangerous bends and no dividers. Slow vehicles like rickshaws and vans run on the same highway with fast buses." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Are the pedestrians free from blame?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Not at all. Many people cross the road carelessly, without using the zebra crossing or the footbridge. Some even talk on the mobile phone while crossing." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Then how can we reduce road accidents?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "First, drivers must be properly trained, and licences should be given only after a strict test. Unfit vehicles must be taken off the road." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "And the traffic laws should be strictly enforced." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Yes. Overspeeding and overloading must be punished. Roads should be widened and repaired, with separate lanes for slow vehicles." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "What can we do as ordinary citizens?" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "We must obey the traffic rules ourselves and make others aware of them. We should not encourage drivers to drive fast, and we should protest when they drive recklessly. Remember, 'Time is valuable, but life is more valuable.'" },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Well said. If everyone is careful, many lives can be saved." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Rafi", text: "Exactly. Now I must go. Goodbye." },
      { type: "dialogue", speaker: "Sakib", text: "Goodbye, and be careful on the road." },
    ],
